# One line. Run from the repo root by `orgasmic verify TASK-CB6GQ`.
#
# The natural red from the TASK-CB6GQ ask, replayed exactly. The injection puts
# both halves of the defect back: `set_section_body` loses its existence check
# and falls through to `upsert_section_text` again (so a write to an unknown
# section silently appends the heading instead of refusing), and the CLI's
# emitted-op set loses `remove_section` (so the daemon accepts an op no verb can
# ask for — a section creatable by typo and removable by nothing).
#
# Both binaries run unconditionally and the exit codes are OR'd, so a failure in
# the first cannot hide the second. Chaining them with `&&` would have stopped
# at the CLI failure and pinned half a proof.
#
# Hermetic: two test binaries. No daemon of the operator's, no tmux, no
# credential, no billed turn — the daemon under test boots in-process on port 0
# against a tempdir home.
cargo test -p orgasmic-cli --bin orgasmic node_edit_op_parity; A=$?; cargo test -p orgasmic-daemon --test node_body_roundtrip; B=$?; exit $((A|B))
